{
  "myth": "In the dawn of the world, Sol held the golden embers of fire, while Terra cradled the seeds of life. Alone, Sol’s heat withered the plains; alone, Terra’s fields remained frozen in shadow. They existed in cold, silent isolation, guarding their own treasures. One epoch, Sol cast a spark into the dark expanse, offering it to the barren ground. Terra, moved by the trust, did not bury the spark but nurtured it, draping the world in vibrant, blossoming greenery. The heat returned to Sol, not as a scorched ember, but as the warmth of life radiating from below. They realized that the spark, once shared, tripled in power through their union. They fashioned a pact: whoever held the surplus would cast it forward, trusting the other to cultivate it. By withholding, they remained stagnant; by giving, they grew prosperous. Thus, the cycle of the seasons was born—a rhythm of trust where the sender’s gift becomes the receiver’s harvest, and the returned fruit sustains the giver. In this dance, they learned that the greatest wealth is not what one keeps, but what one sets in motion, for gold and grain multiply only when they pass between hands."
}

